 NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, San Juan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The ground remains saturated from recent heavy rainfall over the\npast week. After a brief break, deep moisture is expected to\nreturn to southwest Colorado Tuesday with a few inches of\nrainfall possible during the Wednesday through Thursday\ntimeframe. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday through Thursday evening\nproducing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc7a1e63b1aa4908603fa6a6bacfc4eeb0e28910.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cc7a1e63b1aa4908603fa6a6bacfc4eeb0e28910.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-22T05:33:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 220533 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1133 PM MDT Mon Sep 21 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Wetter weather returns to the region by Tuesday, with showers and storms possible each day through the end of the work week. - There is a potential for moderate and heavy rainfall that could lead to flooding mainly in the southern San Juans and surroundin","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-21T21:32:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Dry weather is expected today. Chances for showers and storms increase tomorrow through Thursday. The north